# Database Rules — Eloquent + MySQL

## Key Rules
- Never write raw SQL in business logic — use Eloquent or Query Builder
- Prevent N+1 with eager loading: `Model::with(['relation'])->get()`
- Use `$fillable` on all models for mass assignment protection
- Use `DB::transaction()` for multi-step atomic operations
- Always pagination for lists: `->paginate(20)`

## Eloquent Patterns
```php
// ✅ Select only needed fields
User::select('id', 'email', 'name')->find($id);

// ✅ Eager loading (avoid N+1)
Order::with(['user', 'items.product'])->paginate(20);

// ✅ Transaction
DB::transaction(function () use ($data) {
    $order = Order::create($data);
    Product::where('id', $data['product_id'])->decrement('stock');
});
```

## Migration Conventions
```php
Schema::create('orders', function (Blueprint $table) {
    $table->id();
    $table->foreignId('user_id')->constrained()->cascadeOnDelete();
    $table->decimal('total', 10, 2);
    $table->enum('status', ['pending', 'completed', 'cancelled'])->default('pending');
    $table->softDeletes();
    $table->timestamps();
    $table->index(['user_id', 'created_at']);
});
```

## Commands
```bash
php artisan make:migration create_orders_table
php artisan migrate
php artisan migrate:rollback
php artisan migrate:fresh --seed
```
